WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 11.14 · Fundraising, Revenue & Sustainable Business Models
Investment and repayable finance

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Borrow or invest only where the activity funded generates cash to repay.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Never use repayable finance to cover losses or gaps.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Check what your legal form allows; take independent advice.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Protect control: know lenders’ and investors’ rights before signing.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Vanita Weavers Cooperative (Cooperative · member-owned, India)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Vanita: a four-month US$8,000 loan for festival yarn, repaid from festival sales and sized on confirmed orders only.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You assess whether any repayable finance fits your model.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
